    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0560" n="456" xml:id="pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/137: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-30T10:00:00-05:00">June 30, 1932—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. My telegram No. 109, June 26, 5 p.m., and Department’s telegram No. 45, June
                    29, 5 p.m.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d508-f1"/> Press report dated June 27th was
                    premature but Cabero resigned last night as member of the Junta because of
                    refusal of Junta to adopt his policy of a return to constitutional forms. Eliseo
                    Peña Villalón, a leader in the Radical Socialist Party, takes his place. No
                    other changes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
